      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree adae6b82d23451c4077cf0099429b14614478292\nparent 05bc2f53ce0cb239c17dbdd6b261bd2db7d2a940\nauthor Bruce0X <109469941+Bruce039@users.noreply.github.com> 1790604895 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790604895 -0300\n\nbanman: avoid overflow for large relative ban times\n\nBanMan::Ban adds a relative ban time to GetTime() without a range\ncheck. The offset comes from setban's bantime argument or -bantime,\nand neither has an upper bound, so e.g. `setban <ip> add\n9223372036854775807` overflows int64 (UBSan: \"signed integer overflow\"\nat banman.cpp). In practice the result wraps to a negative nBanUntil,\nthe ban is treated as already expired, and it is silently dropped even\nthough the RPC returns success. With -bantime set that high every\ndefault-duration ban is dropped.\n\nUse SaturatingAdd, so very large ban times are capped at INT64_MAX.",
